WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.430
- Hey, hey, hey, don't
belittle my feelings.

00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:06.118
I'm in a very sensitive place,
and I will kick your ass.

00:00:06.118 --> 00:00:07.400
(audience laughs)

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:08.240
- Oh, come on, Charlie.

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:09.620
So you struck out with a woman.

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:11.150
It happens.

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:13.259
Believe me, it happens.

00:00:13.259 --> 00:00:14.540
(audience laughs)

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:15.960
And when it does, the best thing to do is

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:18.140
to pick yourself up, dust yourself off,

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:20.349
and curse god for making
you the way you are.

00:00:20.349 --> 00:00:21.182
(audience laughs)

00:00:21.182 --> 00:00:23.765
(upbeat music)

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:25.903
- Nice to meet you.

00:00:25.903 --> 00:00:26.780
- Nice to meet you too.

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:28.210
I've heard a lot about you.

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:30.550
- And I've heard a lot about you too.

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:33.437
And I gotta say, I am
pleasantly surprised.

00:00:33.437 --> 00:00:34.890
(audience laughs)

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:35.723
- Really?

00:00:35.723 --> 00:00:36.556
How so?

00:00:36.556 --> 00:00:40.640
- Well, Allen tells me you're
a judge and a professor.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:44.130
And quite frankly I wasn't
expecting someone so uh...

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:47.800
- So what, Charlie?

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:50.509
- Um, yummy.

00:00:50.509 --> 00:00:53.342
(audience laughs)

00:00:58.968 --> 00:01:00.528
That was wrong, wasn't it?

00:01:00.528 --> 00:01:02.370
(audience laughs)

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:03.429
- Yes, that was wrong.

00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:05.057
(audience laughs)

00:01:05.057 --> 00:01:09.520
- What I meant was I was
expecting you to be more,

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:11.419
you know, dry.

00:01:11.419 --> 00:01:12.840
(audience laughs)

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:13.782
But you're not.

00:01:13.782 --> 00:01:16.419
You're actually kind of moist.

00:01:16.419 --> 00:01:18.690
(audience laughs)

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:20.719
Yo, dude, what up?

00:01:20.719 --> 00:01:22.328
(audience laughs)

00:01:22.328 --> 00:01:23.328
Just follow my lead.

00:01:24.659 --> 00:01:26.620
- Ah, this is awesome.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:28.990
- Eh, just a little surf shack

00:01:28.990 --> 00:01:31.520
where I keep my board, beer, and brother.

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:33.310
(audience laughs)

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:35.408
How they breaking today, broheim?

00:01:35.408 --> 00:01:37.190
(audience laughs)

00:01:37.190 --> 00:01:38.390
- How are what breaking?

00:01:39.335 --> 00:01:41.065
- Dude smokes way too much weed.

00:01:41.065 --> 00:01:43.100
(audience laughs)

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:45.340
- The waves, Poindexter.

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:46.683
- Oh, oh, the waves.

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:51.052
The waves are gnarly?

00:01:51.052 --> 00:01:53.320
(audience laughs)

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:54.620
- All right, let's hit it.

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:56.772
- Oh, I intend to.

00:01:56.772 --> 00:01:58.343
(audience laughs)

00:01:58.343 --> 00:02:00.360
(door opens)

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:01.630
Hi Tina.

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:02.860
Long time, huh?

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:04.560
- Charlie Harper.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:05.943
What do you want?

00:02:05.943 --> 00:02:07.430
(audience chuckles)

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:09.669
- I know things didn't
end well between us.

00:02:09.669 --> 00:02:10.502
- Really?

00:02:10.502 --> 00:02:12.300
I thought they ended perfectly.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:15.930
We spent a week in Cancun
having great sex every day.

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:17.060
Flew back to Los Angeles,

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:18.772
you told me you'd call me
tomorrow, and it's been

00:02:18.772 --> 00:02:20.200
what do you know?

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:21.463
A year and a half.

00:02:21.463 --> 00:02:22.296
(audience laughs)

00:02:22.296 --> 00:02:23.800
- Women like Sherry already
know they're beautiful

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:24.633
and desirable.

00:02:24.633 --> 00:02:26.880
You're not gonna score
any points by telling her.

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:27.850
- Okay.

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:29.700
- And don't be in a
hurry to spill your guts.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:31.270
She doesn't need to hear
your whole life story

00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:32.510
before you get to the salad.

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:33.780
- Got it.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:35.490
- And speaking as someone
who knows your life story,

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:37.182
I'd say she doesn't
need to hear it at all.

00:02:37.182 --> 00:02:38.120
(audience laughs)

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:41.684
- Right, right, I'll be
cool, aloof, distant.

00:02:41.684 --> 00:02:42.517
(door bell rings)

00:02:42.517 --> 00:02:44.034
She's here, she's here, she's here.

00:02:44.034 --> 00:02:47.240
(audience laughs)

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:48.930
- Hey Allen, you wanna
catch a movie tonight?

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:49.763
- Can't.

00:02:49.763 --> 00:02:51.620
I am taking a lady friend
to the Hollywood Bowl

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:55.300
for a romantic evening under
the stars with Michael Buble

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.514
and Three Runners Up from American Idol.

00:02:57.514 --> 00:02:59.770
(audience laughs)

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:01.204
- What's in the bag, a noose?

00:03:01.204 --> 00:03:02.820
(audience laughs)

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:04.220
- No, it's a picnic basket.

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:06.700
Fried chicken, bottle of
Merlot, and my autograph hound,

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:07.634
in case I get lucky.

00:03:07.634 --> 00:03:09.100
(audience laughs)

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:13.190
Just out of curiosity, where
do you find women like that?

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:15.010
And more importantly, how
do you get them to go to bed

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:15.843
with you?

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:18.270
- You really want to know?

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:19.620
- Yeah, what's your secret?

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:24.253
- Well, you see, Allen, it's like this.

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:29.204
I got a knack.

00:03:29.204 --> 00:03:32.020
(audience laughs)

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:33.720
- That's not a secret.

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:35.394
- I didn't think so, but you asked.

00:03:35.394 --> 00:03:36.227
(audience laughs)

00:03:36.227 --> 00:03:37.510
- When I'm just dating
one woman at a time,

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:38.410
if she dumps me--

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:39.884
- When she dumps you.

00:03:39.884 --> 00:03:41.290
(audience laughs)

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:43.040
- Either way, I have to start from scratch

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:44.110
finding a new woman.

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:46.030
However, when I'm dating two women,

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:47.030
if one of them dumps me--

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:48.441
- When one of them dumps you.

00:03:48.441 --> 00:03:50.150
(audience laughs)

00:03:50.150 --> 00:03:52.260
- Either way, I'm not alone.

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:54.210
- Wait a second, wait a second,

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:56.030
you're saying that it's advantageous

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:58.023
to date more than one woman at a time?

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:00.842
Good lord, man, you're a genius.

00:04:00.842 --> 00:04:02.330
(audience laughs)

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:03.730
Always break up in a public place.

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:05.120
That way, you avoid having a scene.

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:06.000
- That makes sense.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:08.870
- When, before the dessert menu comes out.

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:10.530
Otherwise, you can find
yourself with a lap full

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:12.771
of hot coffee, which is not
as much fun as it sounds.

00:04:12.771 --> 00:04:13.604
(audience laughs)

00:04:13.604 --> 00:04:14.970
- That doesn't sound fun.

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:16.901
- Sounds fun if you're
wearing a couple of donuts.

00:04:16.901 --> 00:04:20.100
(audience laughs)

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:21.820
- Melissa and I have this chemistry,

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:24.000
and it's really hard not to act on it.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.960
- Yeah, it's tough when you work together.

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:27.510
- Right.

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:28.670
- You don't crap where you eat.

00:04:28.670 --> 00:04:29.529
- I know.

00:04:29.529 --> 00:04:30.730
(audience laughs)

00:04:30.730 --> 00:04:32.421
- You don't dip your pen in company ink.

00:04:32.421 --> 00:04:34.430
(audience laughs)

00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:36.781
And you never bang a woman
who owns a snake or a bird.

00:04:36.781 --> 00:04:40.040
(audience laughs)

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:43.150
After dinner, when you walk
to the car, open her door,

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:46.420
wait for her to say thank
you, smile, lean in,

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:47.580
and kiss her.

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:49.549
- Oh, nice.

00:04:49.549 --> 00:04:52.382
(audience laughs)

00:04:54.722 --> 00:04:56.670
(door opens)

00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:57.820
- Hi, Allen, you ready?

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:00.370
- You're the most beautiful
woman I've ever seen,

00:05:00.370 --> 00:05:01.581
and I don't deserve you.

00:05:01.581 --> 00:05:05.110
(audience screams, laughs, and cheers)

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:07.221
- That's another way to go.

00:05:07.221 --> 00:05:09.804
(upbeat music)